Join Columbia University&amp;rsquo;s M.S. in Nonprofit Management program on Thursday, March 27, at the University&amp;rsquo;s iconic Low Library for &amp;ldquo;Nonprofit and the Arts: Dance Theatre of Harlem,&amp;rdquo; a conversation about nonprofit management, the arts, and the changing landscape featuring M.S. in Nonprofit Management professor of practice and program director Dr. Basil A. Smikle Jr., Dance Theatre of Harlem artistic director Robert Garland, and Dance Theatre of Harlem executive director and NOPM faculty member Anna Glass.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
This event will explore Dance Theatre of Harlem&amp;rsquo;s role as a leading dance institution that encompasses a world-class company, a professional studio, an arts education program, and a community partner.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
